      "locked": false,
      "text": "3. String(char [] ) \n--> Converts character array into string .\n\nex- String city={'B','H','O','P','A','L'};\n\nString str= String (city);\n\nSOP(str); //  BHOPAL\n\n\n4. String( char [] ,int offset ,int count )\n\n--> The constructor String(char[] value, int offset,\nint count) creates a String from a part of a\ncharacter array.\n\nex- \n\nchar[] arr = {'P', 'r', 'a', 't', 'e', 'e', 'k'};\n\nString s = new String(arr, 2, 3);\n\nSystem.out.println(s); // ate",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "3. String(char [] ) \n--> Converts character array into string .\n\nex- String city={'B','H','O','P','A','L'};\n\nString str= String (city);\n\nSOP(str); //  BHOPAL\n\n\n4. String( char [] ,int offset ,int count )\n\n--> The constructor String(char[] value, int offset, int count) creates a String from a part of a character array.\n\nex- \n\nchar[] arr = {'P', 'r', 'a', 't', 'e', 'e', 'k'};\n\nString s = new String(arr, 2, 3);\n\nSystem.out.println(s); // ate",
